CHAPTER VI

SERVICES FOR VICTIMS OF ACTS OF VIOLENCE

Article 17

1. Forms of services provided to Women and Children who are victims of acts of Violence, include:
a. complaint services;
b. health services;
c. legal aid;
d. spiritual counselor services;
e. repatriation and social reintegration; and
f. rehabilitation.
2. Forms of services as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government in cooperation with related Regional Apparatus/institutions are implemented according to minimum service standards established by the Regional Government and implemented by related Regional Apparatus/institutions whose duties and functions are in the fields of:
a. education;
b. manpower;
c. health;
d. social;
e. Women's empowerment and Child protection;
f. mental and spiritual; and
g. public order and peace.
3. In carrying out duties and functions as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government may cooperate with related institutions, other Regional Governments, and community parties.

Article 16

1. Prevention of acts of Violence against Women and Children as referred to in Article 15, is carried out by the PMDP3A Office and Regional Apparatus that administer affairs in the fields of:
a. education;
b. manpower;
c. health;
d. social;
e. women's empowerment and child protection;
f. mental and spiritual;
g. public order and peace; and
h. communication and information.
2. Prevention of acts of Violence by the PMDP3A Office and related Regional Apparatus as referred to in paragraph (1), is carried out in an integrated and continuous manner.

REGENT OF MOROWALI,

Considering:
a. b.
c. d. In view of:
1. 2.

that children and women are creations of God Almighty who constitute important elements of society, and in the future children will become actors in all fields of social and state life;

that Indonesian women have an important role in social activities, development and family life and have the obligation to care for, protect and raise Indonesian children to grow and develop as the nation's next generation;

that based on the Provisions in Article 17 paragraph (Il) of Law Number 23 Year 2074 concerning Regional Government as amended by Law Number 1 Year 2022 concerning Financial Relations between the Central Government and Regional Governments, the Region has the right to establish policies for the protection of women and children which constitute mandatory affairs in accordance with its authority;

that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Protection of Women and Children From Acts of Violence.

CHAPTER V

PREVENTION

Article 15

1. Efforts to prevent Violence against Women and Children are carried out in an integrated manner by the Regional Government coordinated by the PMDP3A Office;
2. Prevention efforts as referred to in paragraph (1) are implemented by:
a. building networks and cooperation with law enforcement apparatus, government apparatus, as well as educational institutions, health institutions, hospitals, various Non-Governmental Organizations concerned with Women and Children;
b. building community and family participation and concern for the prevention and protection of Women and Children from acts of Violence;
c. establishing a violence prevention system that provides a complete and easily accessible information system;
d. conducting socialization about laws and regulations related to the protection of Women and Children who are victims of Violence;
e. providing critical education about the rights of Women and Children as victims of Violence to the community; and
f. opening complaint posts for the protection of Women and Children from acts of Violence.

Article 27

1. The community participates in the provision of protection for victims.
2. Community participation as referred to in paragraph (l) is in the form of: a. forming family partners at the RT/RW or Village level by the community;
b. forming Women and Children protection units within community organizations;
c. conducting independent socialization of Women and Children's rights; d. providing first aid to victims; ande. reporting to the relevant authorized Regional Apparatus/institutions if violence against victims occurs in their environment. (3) Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out by individuals, social community institutions, non-governmental organizations, educational institutions, religious institutions, mental and spiritual development institutions, the private sector, and mass media.

Article 22

1. Rehabilitation services as referred to in Article 17 paragraph (f) letter e include:a. motivation and psychosocial diagnosis;
b. care and nurturing;
c. vocational training and entrepreneurship development;
d. spiritual mental guidance;
e. physical guidance;
f. social guidance and psychosocial counseling;
g. accessibility services;
h. social assistance and aid;
i. resocialization guidance;
j. follow-up guidance; and/ ork. referral.
2. Forms of vocational training and entrepreneurship development as mentioned in paragraph (1) letter c, include:a. skills training;
b. field work practice;
c. apprenticeship;
d. entrepreneurial skills training;
e. facilitation of joint business group formation;
f. business capital in the form of business support tools; andg. business implementation assistance.

Article 2

The scope of regulation for the Protection of Women and Children from acts of violence includes:
a. forms of violence;
b. rights of Women and Children from acts of violence;
c. obligations and responsibilities;
d. prevention;
e. services for victims of acts of Violence;
f. empowerment;
g. cooperation;
h. guidance and Supervision;
i. funding; andj. criminal provisions.
